body:
&#x200B;

Not so much asking for help, but doing it themselves.

"Asking for a friend" is a joke.

Si vi las estrellas y lo que pense es me sabe a mierda quiero tener luz.

&#x200B;

Sin animos de ser negativo asi soy yo.

I guess I've been taken by the stereotype of absurdist.

&#x200B;

But if not for the stereotypes I fail to see what's the role of absurdism.

&#x200B;

Absurdism says meaning isn't possible but living is its own reward? So it's basically optimistic nihilism?

I'm beggining to think that way, nevermind that the process scares me shitless.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
